    {
      "id": "ADM-39",
      "question": "How long may a client who has paid in full wait for the next stage to open before somebody is told?",
      "blocks": [
        "G-073",
        "G-080"
      ],
      "why": "D18 gave the retry ladder ~19 minutes of real spacing. After that the job is dead and nothing tries again. The ladder is an engineering default; the number is a business rule nobody has stated."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADM-40",
      "question": "Is supabase/_bundle.sql a supported install path?",
      "blocks": [
        "G-085"
      ],
      "why": "It is twelve migrations stale and ships the D19 defect. Either CI regenerates it on every migration, or it is deleted and `db push` is documented as the only way in. Keeping it as-is means the documented install produces a knowingly defective deployment."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADM-41",
      "question": "Does winning a deal qualify its lead, or must a lead be qualified before a deal can be won?",
      "blocks": [
        "G-075",
        "G-086"
      ],
      "why": "Nothing requires a lead to be qualified before a deal is opened on it, so the ordinary path is new -> deal won -> converted. LEAD_TRANSITIONS says only qualified may become converted. Both cannot be true. D20 preserved today's behaviour rather than pick."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADM-42",
      "question": "When a past client comes back, is that a new deal on the same lead, or a new lead?",
      "blocks": [
        "G-076",
        "G-088"
      ],
      "why": "WhatsApp ingest keys a lead to a phone number permanently, so a returning client lands on the same lead row. D21 stopped the schema from forbidding a second deal there, but createOpportunity still returns the settled one instead of raising a new one. Which behaviour is right is a sales-process question."
    }
  ],
